  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the strong electrolytes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></math>. Limiting molar conductivity&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>440</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, respectively. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is</p><p>Given:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Ion</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mmultiscripts><mo>&#160;</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is the limiting molar conductivity of ions</p><p>The plot of molar conductivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#923;</mi></mfenced></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math> is given below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/8f22ac03-49c6-47b4-86b9-9e69736b0508-image.png\" style=\"width: 303px; height: 270px;\" /></p><p>If the numerical value has more than two decimal places, truncate/round-off the value to TWO decimal places.</p>",
